    q: "Which commerce routes have a capped salary ladder?",
    a: "Bank PO and clerk posts and RBI Grade B pay on a published scale, so the ceiling is known in advance. A general degree with no added skill also sits on a flat band. A side route can add income where service rules allow it.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I earn from commerce skills while studying?",
    a: "Yes, where work is small and visible, such as bookkeeping, GST filing support, a report for a shop, or a simple campaign. Start with one clear job and one pleased client. Never count on a fixed income. Treat the first paid project as proof, not as a salary.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does an economics degree pay more than BCom?",
    a: "We found no reliable survey of economics entry pay, so we make no claim. Economics opens research, policy and data roles and the RBI Grade B DEPR stream, which had 10 posts in 2026. Statistics and coding skill will move pay more than the degree name.",
  },
  {
    q: "Will AI cut commerce salaries?",
    a: "It is cutting clerical entry first. The World Economic Forum lists accounting, bookkeeping and payroll clerks and bank tellers among the fastest-declining roles worldwide. Advice, review, analysis and client work are safer and can be sped up with AI. Learn to use AI and to check its output.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is it worth borrowing for a commerce degree or course?",
    a: "Usually not. As a strict planning rule, keep college to about 10% of your total education budget and treat 20% as a caution line. Avoid education debt unless a credential is legally required. ICAI registration fees across three levels add up to Rs 49,000, so the larger costs are coaching and repeat attempts.",
  },
  {
    q: "How reliable are the pay figures in this guide?",
    a: "Every figure is an indicative range or average, tied to a named source and date, and none is exact or guaranteed. Where no sample existed, the page says so instead of printing a number. Look at live job listings and talk to people in the role before you decide.",
  },
];

