>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>Commerce career options with salary run from about Rs 18,000 a month for a typical graduate in formal work to Rs 12 to 13 lakh a year for a placed, newly qualified CA, and the gap comes from the route you take, not from the commerce stream.</strong>
    The right early decisions, and a high-income skill portfolio built beside the degree, are what unlock the higher band and earlier financial freedom. This guide prices each route in rupees, years and risk.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A plain BA, BSc, BCom or BBA graduate in formal work earns a median of Rs 18,000 a month at entry and Rs 25,000 at three or more years (PLFS 2025). Only 9.6% of those formal workers earn Rs 50,000 a month or more by then.</li>
      <li><strong>Lead with routes that can scale: finance and data analytics, digital growth, and an accounts, tax and GST practice. CA, CS and CMA are credentials with a business layer but a long ladder. Bank and RBI routes pay on a published scale, so the top is known in advance.</strong></li>
      <li>Before you trust any commerce pay number, run it through The 3-Clock Check: the exam clock, the low-pay clock and the payoff clock.</li>
      <li>Keep the degree, add one pay skill, and decide on a professional course only after you have priced all three clocks.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>
